From: x86.mov movfuscator-wasm
Subject: [PATCH] libiberty: make psignal's message parameter `const char *`

Emscripten's <signal.h> declares `psignal(int, const char *)`. libiberty's
fallback definition omits the const, so when compiling for wasm via emcc
it conflicts with the platform header and the build aborts.

This patch applies to the libiberty stub itself, not to any consumer.
The libiberty implementation is only reached when HAVE_PSIGNAL isn't
defined — but even on hosts where it is defined, the prototype must
still match the platform's. Adding const is strictly safer.

--- a/libiberty/strsignal.c
+++ b/libiberty/strsignal.c
@@ -551,7 +551,7 @@
 #ifndef HAVE_PSIGNAL
 
 void
-psignal (int signo, char *message)
+psignal (int signo, const char *message)
 {
   if (signal_names == NULL)
     {
